Known failure: range-stable — a statement left without ";" before :ELSE / :OTHERWISE is terminated by range formatting but not by the full formatter (#326 item 1)
Known failure: no-gained-errors — an unterminated :EXITCASE before :OTHERWISE stays unterminated, adding exitcase_last_in_branch (#326)
Lines that finish a statement without `;` get one when the next line
starts a new statement: after an identifier, number, string, closing
delimiter, postfix `++` (issue #99), a code-block literal and a bare
keyword (fmt.semicolon_enforcement). `:BEGINCASE` always ends with `;`.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Terminate
:PARAMETERS nValue
:DECLARE sLabel, aList, fnDouble, nCount
nCount := 0
sLabel := "start"
aList := {1, 2}
fnDouble := {|n| n * 2}
nCount++
:BEGINCASE
:CASE nValue == 1
sLabel := Upper(sLabel)
:EXITCASE
:OTHERWISE
sLabel := ""
:EXITCASE
:ENDCASE
:RETURN sLabel
:ENDPROC
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Terminate;
	:PARAMETERS nValue;
	:DECLARE sLabel, aList, fnDouble, nCount;
	nCount := 0;
	sLabel := "start";
	aList := {1, 2};
	fnDouble := {|n| n * 2};
	nCount++;
	:BEGINCASE;
	:CASE nValue == 1;
		sLabel := Upper(sLabel);
		:EXITCASE
	:OTHERWISE;
		sLabel := "";
		:EXITCASE;
	:ENDCASE;
	:RETURN sLabel;
:ENDPROC;
